+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop on Lantern Row in
+the market town of Little Hadley. It has a home page, a browsable catalogue with genre
+filters, an events list, and a visit page with opening hours, directions and a contact form.
+
+The site is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. There is no build step, no framework and no
+runtime dependencies. It makes no requests outside its own origin: no CDNs, web fonts,
+analytics or remote images.
+
+## Running it locally
+
+Serve the repository root with any static server, then open the printed address:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8080
+# then open http://localhost:8080/
+```
+
+`npx http-server -p 8080 -s .` works too. Pages use relative links, so the site also works
+when it is deployed under a sub-path.
+
+## File layout
+
+```
+index.html          Home: intro, featured books, next events, hours summary
+books.html          Catalogue with genre filters (state kept in ?genre=...)
+events.html         Upcoming and past events
+visit.html          Opening hours, address, access notes, contact form
+css/styles.css      The one shared stylesheet (colours are CSS custom properties)
+js/books-data.js    The book catalogue (single source of truth)
+js/events-data.js   The events list (single source of truth)
+js/events-logic.js  Local-date helpers: upcoming/past split and date formatting
+js/event-item.js    Builds one event list item
+js/book-card.js     Builds one book card and its SVG cover
+js/books.js         Books page: filtering, URL state and the live result count
+js/events.js        Events page
+js/home.js          Home page featured books and event teaser
+js/contact.js       Contact form validation and the demo confirmation
+js/nav.js           Shared menu toggle for narrow screens
+tests/              Headless-browser tests (node:test + Playwright)
+```
+
+To add a book or event, edit the data file. Every page that shows them renders from there.
+
+## Running the tests
+
+The tests start their own static server on an ephemeral port and drive headless Chromium
+through Playwright. They expect Playwright to be installed globally, for example at
+`/opt/node-tools/node_modules/playwright`. The helper falls back to `npm root -g` to find it.
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/*.test.mjs            # all tests
+node --test tests/books.test.mjs        # one file
+npx prettier --check "**/*.{html,css,js,mjs}"   # formatting
+```
+
+The event tests fix the clock to 17 November 2026 with Playwright's clock API, so their results
+do not depend on the real date.
